                  \\right)
          %p
            A priori this yields a
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1#SequentialTSpectra"} sequential S2-spectrum
            = succeed "-spectrum" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            with those in even degree.
          %p
            This represents a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            and indeed the universal one among these, see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+complex+orientation+on+MU"} universal complex orientation on MU
          %p
            The
            %em periodic
            complex cobordism theory is given by adding up all the even degree powers of this theory:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi P
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∨
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M P = \vee_{n \in \mathbb{Z}} \Sigma^{2 n} M U
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M P({*})
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard+ring"} Lazard ring
            which is the universal coefficient ring for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+laws"} formal group laws
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Milnor-Quillen+theorem+on+MU"} Milnor-Quillen theorem on MU
            \.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+cohomology+theory"} periodic
            version is sometimes written
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PMU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PMU
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#HomotopyGroups Homotopy groups: Cobordism and Lazard ring
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+ring"} graded ring
            given by evaluating complex cobordism theory on the point is both the complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
            as well as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard+ring"} Lazard ring
            classifying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+laws"} formal group laws
          #RelationToCobordismRing.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Evaluation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
              on the point yields the complex
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mi MU
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi MU
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi pt
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_\ast MU \simeq MU_\ast(pt) \simeq \mathbb{Z}[x_1, x_2, \cdots]
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the generator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
              is in degree
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 i
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Milnor60"}> Milnor 60
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Novikov60"} Novikov 60
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Novikov62"} Novikov 62
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Ravenel"} Ravenel theorem 1.2.18
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Ravenel"} Ravenel, ch. 3, theorem 3.1.5
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+law"} formal group law
            associated with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            as with any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            is classified by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi MU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \longrightarrow \pi_\bullet(MU)
            out of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard+ring"} Lazard ring
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              This canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi MU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} \pi_\bullet(MU)
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard+ring"} Lazard ring
              and the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi MU
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RelationToCobordismRing"}
              with the complex
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen%27s+theorem+on+MU"} Quillen's theorem on MU
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LurieLect7"} Lurie 10, lect. 7, theorem 1
          %h3#UniversalComplexOrientation
            Universal complex orientation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U
          %p
            There is a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex orientation
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            obtained from the map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega : \mathbb{C}P^\infty \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                  M U(1)
                  \\;\;\;\;
                  M U(\mathbb{C}P^\infty)
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy-commutative+ring+spectrum"} homotopy-commutative ring spectrum
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex orientation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            maps of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MU
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi E
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  MU \longrightarrow E
                  \\,.
          %p
            (e.g
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#LurieLect6"} Lurie 10, lect. 6, theorem 8
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Ravenel"} Ravenel, chapter 4, lemma 4.1.13
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+orientation+and+MU"} complex orientation and MU
          %h3#homology_of_a_manifold_bordisms_in_
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            \-homology of a manifold: bordisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "-homology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi MU
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU_\ast(X)
            of its underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            is the group of equivalence classes of maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to X
            from manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
            on the stable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Ravenel"} Ravenel chapter 1, section 2
          %p
            For more information, see the article
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+homology+theory"} bordism homology theory
          %h3#cohomology_of_a_manifold_cobordisms_in_
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            \-cohomology of a manifold: cobordisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            \-cohomology groups of a manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            can be expressed in terms of bordisms given by proper
            %a{:href => "cobordism+cohomology+theory#ComplexOrientedMaps"} complex-oriented maps
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %p
            For more information, see the article
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
          %h3#homology_of__hopf_algebroid_structure_on_dual_steenrod_algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            \-homology of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
          %p
            Moreover, the dual
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steenrod+algebra"} Steenrod algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi MU
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi MU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU_\bullet(MU)
            forms a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebroid"} commutative Hopf algebroid
            over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard+ring"} Lazard ring
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landweber-Novikov+theorem"} Landweber-Novikov theorem
          %h3#nilpotence_theorem Nilpotence theorem
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotence+theorem"} nilpotence theorem
          %h3#snaiths_theorem Snaith’s theorem
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snaith%27s+theorem"} Snaith's theorem
            asserts that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+complex+cobordism+spectrum"} periodic complex cobordism spectrum
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+%E2%88%9E-ring"} ∞-group ∞-ring
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for stable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            (the classifying space for
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+element"} Bott element
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PMU
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi β
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  PMU \simeq \mathbb{S}[B U][\beta^{-1}]
                  \\,.
          %h3#localization_and_brownpeterson_spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            \-Localization and Brown-Peterson spectrum
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-localization"} p-localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            decomposes into the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown-Peterson+spectra"} Brown-Peterson spectra
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cobordism+cohomology"} differential cobordism cohomology
          %div
            %p
              %strong>
                flavors of
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+homology+theories"} bordism homology theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theories"} cobordism cohomology theories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} representing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectra"} Thom spectra
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+rings"} cobordism rings
              \:
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+homology+theory"} bordism theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M%28B%2Cf%29"} M(B,f)
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-bordism"}> B-bordism
              ):
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MFr"} MFr
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MO"}> MO
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSO"} MSO
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSpin"} MSpin
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MString"} MString
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"}> MU
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSU"} MSU
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ravenel%27s+spectrum"} MΩΩSU(n)
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MP-theory"}> MP
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MR-theory"} MR
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSpin%5Ec"}
                    MSpin
                    %sup
                      %i c
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSp"} MSp
            %p relative bordism theories:
